# AutoOS installer/rescue USB — sanitised Debian-installer preseed template.
#
# Companion to templates/user-data.example for media that still boot the
# classic Debian Installer instead of Ubuntu's subiquity/autoinstall. The
# same two hard rules apply here as everywhere else in this repository
# (AGENTS.md):
#
#   1. No real secret ships in this file. Every value that looks like it
#      should be private is the literal placeholder CHANGE-ME-AT-CREATION-TIME,
#      substituted at USB-creation time — see the account-setup section below.
#   3. No disk is wiped without the operator asking for it — see the
#      partitioning section below.

### Localization
d-i debian-installer/locale string en_US.UTF-8
d-i keyboard-configuration/xkb-keymap select us

### Network
d-i netcfg/choose_interface select auto
d-i netcfg/get_hostname string autoos-rescue
d-i netcfg/get_domain string unassigned-domain

### Account setup
# A full SHA-512 crypt hash, never a plaintext password. The USB-creation
# tool replaces CHANGE-ME-AT-CREATION-TIME with the hash of a freshly
# generated passphrase (shown to the operator exactly once, B7), produced by
# `openssl passwd -6` — falling back to `mkpasswd -m sha512crypt` — and it
# refuses to write this file at all if neither tool is present (B12). Do not
# hand-roll SHA-512-crypt: Python's `crypt` module is POSIX-only and was
# removed in Python 3.13, and getting the algorithm subtly wrong by hand is
# exactly how the previous incident happened — a committed plaintext password
# (A1) next to a hash truncated to 82 of the required 86 characters (A2),
# which locks you out of the machine you just installed.
d-i passwd/user-fullname string AutoOS Rescue
d-i passwd/username string rescue
d-i passwd/user-password-crypted password CHANGE-ME-AT-CREATION-TIME
d-i passwd/root-login boolean false

### Partitioning — INTERACTIVE BY DEFAULT.
#
# partman-auto/method is left UNSET on purpose: an installer with no
# partman-auto/method stops and asks a human to lay out partitions by hand,
# same as a manual install. This is the direct fix for A3, where the original
# scripts wiped the whole target disk automatically with no prompt at all,
# and it matches AGENTS.md hard rule 3 ("every destructive action is opt-in
# and announced").
#
# Only when the operator explicitly passed --wipe-target-disk at USB-creation
# time (recorded by the creation tool as AUTOOS_WIPE_TARGET_DISK) does the
# generator uncomment a block shaped like the one below, with the disk field
# filled in from the disk the operator confirmed — named by model and size in
# full, e.g. "Samsung 980 PRO 1TB (/dev/nvme0n1) will be ERASED" — never a
# bare "largest disk" guess.
#
# d-i partman-auto/disk string CHANGE-ME-AT-CREATION-TIME
# d-i partman-auto/method string regular
# d-i partman-auto/choose_recipe select atomic
# d-i partman-partitioning/confirm_write_new_label boolean true
# d-i partman/choose_partition select finish
# d-i partman/confirm boolean true
# d-i partman/confirm_nooverwrite boolean true

### Base system / packages
tasksel tasksel/first multiselect standard, ssh-server
d-i pkgsel/include string openssh-server

### Finish
d-i finish-install/reboot_in_progress note
